            "intro-date-title": "The night sky on any date",
            "intro-date": "By default the map shows the sky right now, as seen from your location. Set a date and time, such as a birthday or the night of an upcoming meteor shower, to see how the sky looked or will look at that moment. Speed up time to watch constellations rise and set through the night.",
            "intro-location": "The observing location comes from geolocation or can be set by hand, so the map works for any city. Search finds stars, constellations, planets and deep-sky objects.",
